"1 north gates"
"Looming off to the north are the stone gates of the city; their white

marble bricks standing out against the green background.  Atop each side

of the gates are stone watchtowers in which you can see small shapes

moving about.

"
E
"wagon ruts"
"Each of the wagon ruts that scar the surface of the road are about three

inches deep.  The bottom of the ruts are filled with a small layer of mud

as well as some bits of gravel.  The grass around the edge of them has

been trampled by the many feet that have walked across this point.

