#76753
"North Main Street"
"The street here is covered with deep wagon ruts that have filled with

water from past rains, leaving puddles of mud everywhere.  Sitting just

off the street to the east and west are small stone houses with wide

gravel walkways leading up to them.  Around the foundations of each house

are small white lilies and red rose bushes.  To the south North Main

Street continues its course into the heart of the city towards a small

hill.  To the north the street makes its way towards the northern gates

of the city.

"
