"1 east west stone houses"
"Standing off the edge of the street to the east and west are small,

thatched roof stone cottages.  Both hoses are nearly identical; each have

white marble walls, two windows and a single, small door.  Small, grey

rock gravel walkways lead up to the doors of each house.  Around the base

of the walls are several rows of white lilies as well as some roses

bushes.

"
E
"gravel walkways"
