#76763
"North Main Street"
"Most of the grass along this strip of the street has been ripped away by

the many feet that tread down this road everyday.  In place of the grass

are large mud puddles which span almost the entire width of the road. 

Standing just off the street to the west is a large white marble building. 

Great stone pillars line the front of the building and support its

massive domed ceiling.  Directly to the east an open archway leads into a

small, brightly-lit stone building.  To the south the street climbs up a

sloping hill onto Sunnydale Park.  To the north the street continues its

course through the city.

"
