"grass street"
"This strip of road is void of any grass, having been ripped away by years

of travellers treading across it.  In place of the grass are large mud

puddles which span across the width of the road.

"
E
"mud puddles"
"These large mud puddles are a dark brown color and some have taken on the

color of the soil; a rich black color.  Each of the puddles are mere

inches from one another.  The large puddles span the entire width of the

road, leading right up to the doorways of two stone buildings to the east

and west.

"
