#76767
"Baker's Way"
"Standing just off the road to the north and south are two large marble

buildings with thick, thatched roofs.  Small alleyways run past each of

the buildings in which you can see several large crates and sacks stacked

up next to them.  The sound of roaring flames can be clearly heard from

within each of the structures and the distinct aroma of chocolate, sugar

and vanilla wafts out from within them.  The grassy road continues to the

east and west from here, continuing past the many bakeries of the town.

"
