#76770
"Baker's Way"
"Small walls composed of blocks of white marble line the edges of Baker's

Way here.  Wagon ruts can be clearly seen imprinted into the soft, grassy

ground.  Dotting the road are several small white lilies which have

avoided being crushed by the traffic this road has seen.  To the east a

small hill rises up from the center of town on which you can see several

white benches surrounding a large crystal fountain.  To the west Baker's

Way continues as it runs in between several buildings lining its edges.

"
