#76771
"Baker's Way"
"Large wagons filled to their tops with large crates, sacks, and barrels

sit just off the edge of the road.  Patches of grass have been torn free

from the road from several years of feet constantly walking upon it and

the many wagons which come through the town.  To the north stands a large

building with a low archway from which the scent of cheese emanates.  A

small building topped with four small chimneys, each spewing forth

billowing clouds of black smoke, stands directly to your south.  Baker's

Way continues to the east and west from this point as it continues its

course through the town.

"
