"wagons crates sacks barrels"
"Large wooden wagons have been placed just off the edge of the road to the

south, between the gaps in the buildings.  Stored neatly in the back of

each wagon are several large wooden crates stamped with the seal of

Shadybrook.  Burlap sacks labeled \"Sugar\" and \"Flour\" have been stacked

next to the crates.  A few capped, iron-banded barrels have also been

placed in the wagons but their contants remain unknown.

"
