#76772
"Intersection of Emerald Avenue and Baker's Way"
"Two roads intersect at this point in town, Emerald Avenue and Baker's Way. 

Most of the grass which covers the intersection has been crushed beneath

the weight of wagons and the many feet of travellers passing over this

point but on each corner of the roads it grows thick and tall.  Looming

like a watchful guardian directly to the west are the western gates of

the city.  Atop each side of the gates are small stone watchtowers in

which you can just barely make out the movement of guards.  Emerald

Avenue runs to the north and south, and Baker's Way heads east.

"
