"South Main Street"
"Towering up before you to the east and west are massive two-story stone

buildings with thick, thatched roofs.  Rich, brown maple support beams

have been worked into the corners of the buildings and the stones set in

between them.  Several windows adorn the faces of the walls and peering

inside you can see several halflings gathered at the tables inside. 

Engraved bronze @Ysigns@n hang over the doors of each dwelling upon which

you can see bold writing.  Off in the distance to the south the massive

southern gates of the city can be seen.  South Main Street continues to

the north and south from this point as it continues through the town.

