#76784
"Intersection of Sunnydale Lane and Wildflower Lane"
"Sunndydale Lane and Wildflower Lane intersect with each other at this

point.  In the center of the road is a towering oak tree which stands at

least thirty feet high.  It rich, dark brown bark is mottled with bits of

green moss.  At the base of the tree, someone has taken the time to plant

small yellow lilacs and pink daisies.  Wagon ruts run around each side of

the tree, heading off in every direction.  Directly to the east the

massive eastern gates of the city rise up.  Sunnydale Lane heads west as

it makes its way back into the center of the city.  Wildflower Lane

continues its north-south course from this point.

"
