E
"large holes avenue road street"
"These large pot holes have been left over time from the many feet as well

as wagon wheels passing down this avenue.  Each has filled with thick,

brown mud from the past rains the area has seen.

"
E
"wagon ruts"
"Each of the wagon ruts are about five inches deep and lying at their

bottom are small pools of muddy water.  Most of the ruts are fairly new

judging by the fresh soil which has been thrown up alongside them.

"
E
"1 south trench"
"The trench runs along the base of the city walls to the south for about

eight feet.  Each is filled with thick, brown mulch and dark soil.  Large

holes have been dug within the trench every two feet and resting beside

them are clay pots which contain young shrubs.

"
E
"clay pots shrubs"
"The clay pots are of simple design and have no distinguishing features. 

Within each of them is a young shrub with lush green leaves.  A few of

the shrubs have tiny white flowers hanging from their branches which

emanate a pleasant aroma.

"
E
"stone watchtower"
"From this distance the watchtower appears as nothing more than a mound of

white stone with some type of banner flying above it.

"
