#76791
"Sugarloaf Street"
"A row of large birch trees line the soutern edge of the road; their

massive trunks pressing against the city walls.  Scattered all about the

base of the trees are patches of wildflowers of various colors.  Along

the northern edge of the road are several small statues carved in the

likeness of halflings bedecked in battle-worn armor.  To the northeast a

large two-story building rises up between two small hills.  To the

northwest stands a smaller building topped with a brightly-colored banner. 

The street continues to climb and descend along the small hills as it

heads east and west.

