#76792
"Sugarloaf Street"
"Two large wagons sit off the northern edge of the street here; their

drivers no where in sight and their cargo holds empty.  Stacked up in a

neat pile next to the wagons are a mound of white stone blocks and a

large barrel filled with a thick, grey substance.  A small gravel

footpath leads off to the northwest around the base of large two-story

building which towers directly to the north.  The grass-covered street

heads off to the east and west continuing its long course around the

outskirts of the city.

