#76793
"Sugarloaf Street"
"Standing directly to the north of you is a large two-story stone building. 

Dark maple beams have been set into the corners of it on which hang

glass-covered lanterns.  Several small windows adorn the face of the

building within which you can see several vague shapes moving about.  Off

to the southeast you catch a glimpse of the mighty stone gates of the

city.  Like a guardian watching over you, the thick city walls never

stray from their straight east-west expanse along the southern edge of

the avenue.  To the east and west the street continues to make its way

about the city.

