#76798
"Corner of Wildflower Lane and Sugarloaf Street"
"Wildflower Lane's southern journey comes to an abrupt halt here, stopped

by the looming city walls.  At the corner of the walls above, you can see

a raised banner flapping proudly in the air.  Growing at the bottom

corner of the walls are several bushes shaped in the figure of a pony,

rabbit, and dog.  Looking north, the avenue passes by a row of small

houses.  To the west, Sugarloaf Street begins its advance through town,

becoming slightly more level and the grass seems to grow slightly taller

in that direction.

"
