#76799
"Wildflower Lane"
"Numerous leafy bushes and broad ferns line the sides of the avenue here. 

Just off the avenue to the west is a small purple cottage.  Two heart-

shaped shutters beside the window have been opened, and a rectangular pot

of flowers has been placed near its sill.  Looming over the cottage is a

maple tree that shades the house from most sunlight.  Hanging from the

tree's largest branch is a wide wooden plank that is tied to the branch

by two sturdy-looking ropes.  The lane continues further north beside

more houses and reaches a bend to the south.

