#76807
"Emerald Avenue"
"Small clumps of moss have started to grow along the towering city wall to

the west.  The shape of the clumps resemble small round pies due to their

semi-circular ridges.  Stacked along the base of the wall in a four by

four configuration are some blocks of white marble that contain several

long cracks about half an inch wide.  Off to the east is a peculiar-

looking building, but you see no way to enter it from here.  The avenue

extends to the north and south, where the grass continues to grow

abundantly and almost totally blankets the tilted ground.

