"grey rocks grass avenue"
"These large, grey rocks vary in size; some the size of a halfling's skull

while others rival a storm giant's head.  Their surface is very smooth

and is specked with white dots.

"
E
"wagon ruts"
"Several wagon ruts scar the surface of the avenue; some very old while

others look to be recently made.  The ruts lead right up to a group of

grey rocks, head over them, and than continue on the other side.

"
E
"weeds flowers"
"Thick ragweeds grow along each side of this stretch of the avenue,

mingling with small patches of wildflowers.  The weeds have begun to

snake their way around the stems of the flowers in a vain attempt to

destroy them.

"
