E
"southern wall shields bucklers tower"
"The entire southern wall is covered with shields of every size, shape,

color and metal.  The shields range from simple bronze bucklers to

colorfully painted kite shields.  One shield catches your eye; resting in

the center of all the others is a massive adamantite tower shield

emblazoned with the image of a red dragon a stream of fire.

"
E
"western wall shelves helms"
"The helms which rest atop the shelves along the western wall are of

superior design.  Each has been carefully polished and kept free of any

tarnish or rust.  Ivory greathelms and bronze caps are just a few of the

helms which the armorsmiths of Shadybrook have put on display in this

shop.

"
E
"eastern wall suits armor plate"
"The entire eastern wall is a sheet of metal.  Plate mail crafted in

unique shapes and colorfully painted have been hung from the wall.  Each

suit is sized for different races from someone the size of a halfling to

an ent.  Each suit has been carefully polished to a high shine causing

your reflection to be easily seen upon its surface.

"
E
"stone table"
"This stone table is of simple design; a stone slab carefully carved to

remove its sharp edges mounted atop a solid stone block.  Cluttered

across the table are several polishing cloths, glass vials of oil used to

help keep the platemail rust-free and a large blacksmith's hammer used

for banging dents out.

"
