#76826
"Shadybrook Militia's Barracks"
"This small building is nothing more than a hollow shell; the walls are

utterly bare of any decorations.  What little lies in the room is nothing

spectacular; a small table with four wooden chairs sits against the

northern wall and a wooden weapons rack filled with spears is set against

the eastern wall.  A small fireplace which burns with small flames has

been set against the western wall provides the only light for the room. 

In the center of the room a small black hole leads deep into the ground. 

Attached to the floor next the hole is a steel ladder which descends into

the darkness.  To the south a heavy steel door leads out onto Jezebel

Avenue.

"
