#76827
"On a Steel Ladder"
"Dark, dirt walls surround you in every direction, closing in to mere

inches from your body at some points.  Twisted roots protrude from the

walls and run down the length of them.  The steel ladder bolted to the

southern wall is covered in bits of grime which make some of the steps

extremely slippery, causing you to hang on tight for fear of falling off. 

Below you the ladder descends into darkness and even the glint of its

steel cannot be seen.  Above you the ladder rises towards a small

opening, leading into a dimly lit room.

"
