#76828
"A Dark and Silent Earthen Room"
"This small, cold room has been dug straight through the dirt beneath the

city.  The walls are nothing but packed dirt with a few wooden support

beams occasionally set up at weak points.  The ground is scarred by deep

ruts, left over time by the many feet which passed through this area.  To

the north a row of torches line the walls of a passageway as it heads

through the barracks.  To the east and west small doors have been set

into the earthen walls, leading to seperate chambers.  A heavy steel

ladder has been tacked to the southern wall, extending upwards into a

dark shaft.

"
