#76831
"Enlisted Men's Bunkhouse"
"Small bunkbeds line the walls of this small dirt chamber, each covered

with thick woolen blankets and clean uniforms.  The air is fairly damp

and cold, making this room bunkhouse a very uncomfortable living area.  A

grey stone fireplace has been carved into a gap in the western wall and

despite its blazing flames it barely lets off enough heat to break

through the biting cold.  Hanging from the southern wall is a tattered

silk tapestry with the image of two crossed swords upon it.  Set into the

eastern wall is a small oak door, covered in a thin green moss, which

leads back out of the bunkhouse.

"
