#76846
"Shadybrook Jeweler's Market"
"This spacious building is made entirely from white obsidian blocks which

have been polished to a high shine.  The dome-style roof is plated in

gold and a mural of halfling gem cutters at work has been etched into its

surface.  The walls of the building have had stone shelves placed all

along them atop which rest gemworking supplies ranging from polishing

cloths to steel files.  In the center of the room is a glass display

case, lined with a soft red velvet cloth.  Housed inside the case are

several different types of exotic gems and jewerly.  To the west an

archway carved in the shape of two halflings with their swords crossed

above their heads marks the only exit back onto Jezebel Avenue.

