"Before the Altar of Freylia"
"Set against the northern wall of this brightly-lit chamber is a massive

altar composed of white obsidian slabs; each polished to a high shine. 

Etched along the faces of each of the slabs are carvings of halflings at

play, work and battle.  Scattered across the altar are several types of

offerings ranging from freshly-baked tarts to baskets of wildflowers.  On

each side of the altar is a life-like granite statue carved into the

likeness of the goddess.  Hanging from the eastern and western walls are

enormous silk tapestries portraying Freylia healing fallen halfling

warriors.  Ruby-encrusted braziers, each ablaze with violet-hued flames,

line the walls of the room leading straight up to the altar.  To the

south a small passage leads away from the altar.

