"The Dancing Kobold Inn - Dining Area"
"Finely crafted redwood tables covered in red tablecloths have been set up

in a neat pattern about the room.  Four cushioned wooden chairs surround

each of the tables.  Resting in the center of the tables are brass

candles holders each containing a tallow candle which burns with a dull

flame.  The floor is carpeted with a fine silken rug with the image of a

waterfall rushing down over a snow-capped mountain embroidered upon its

surface.  Upon the western wall is a large @Mmenu@n written on

tan-colored paper.  Lying off in the room to the north is a small bar

with several stools resting before it.  To the east lies the entranceway

into the inn.

