#76870
"Northern Watchtower"
"This stone watchtower gives an excellent view of the surrounding wilds,

allowing the watchmen of the city of view threats coming from any angle. 

The grassy, rolling hills of the wilds stretch out to the northeast and

northwest of you, going on for several miles.  Directly to the west, just

below you, are the northern gates of the city behind which you can see

the gate guards standing.  Set against the southern wall is an open

iron-bound chest filled with crossbow bolts, spears and flasks of oil

attached to rags.  To the east a small stone door leads out onto the

battlements surrounding the city.  Set against the northern edge of the

tower is a stone staircase leading down into the guard house.

"
